<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The Shipcracker armor's jump, templated from VFEP's VFEP_PowerJump (1.6/Defs/AbilityDefs/
    Abilities.xml). The rules live in ShipcrackerWarcasket.Ability_BreachJump (planet: ranged,
    no sight test; space: unlimited range, sight required; landing-only blast), the numbers in
    the BreachJumpExtension below. requireLineOfSight is ignored by the
    ability class and set false only to document the planet rule. gizmoClass adds the
    "jumps / max" count in the button's top-right corner, where vanilla's jump pack shows its own.

    The mod settings (Source/1.6/Settings/) take their defaults from the extension's fuel,
    blast, damage and roof numbers, cooldownTime (unset, so none), the armor's tank size and
    range offset, the shoulders' breach power and SCWC_Breach's structure factors, and write
    the player's values over them.

    fuelPerJump 20 chemfuel of the armor's 100-charge chemfuel tank: Aerial's numbers, 5
    jumps. It stays in chemfuel when the VGE root switches the tank to astrofuel; that root
    sets chemfuelPerAmmo instead.
    breachDamage 20 is the pawn-facing number (Aerial's jump 15, a frag grenade 50); building
    damage and wound splitting come from the SCWC_Breach DamageDef. breachArmorPenetration 0.15
    (Aerial's works out at 0.225, a grenade's 0.75) is passed explicitly because GenExplosion
    otherwise derives it as damage x 0.015; the 1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root sets it
    in CE's megapascals. breachRadius 2 is a 13-cell footprint: a door-sized
    hole in the wall it lands beside (vanilla's explosion also hits walls adjacent to the open
    cells it reaches) rather than a leveled room. Wearer excluded; allies are not, as with
    Aerial. roofPunchRadius 1 keeps the ceiling hole tighter than the wall hole; in
    space that vents the gravship room the wearer leaves or breaches into. A radius of 0
    turns the blast or the roof punch off.

    Space flight runs at spaceFlightSpeedFactor 3 times the wearer's VFEP_FlightSpeed (36
    cells/s at the base 12; Aerial's full set reaches 27 on a planet), capped at
    spaceFlightMaxSeconds 4 so a hop past 144 cells speeds up rather than drags.

    vacuumLabel "breach burn" replaces the label in space (gizmo and tooltip title), and
    spaceIconPath the icon. The description carries no numbers (VEF appends range, radius and
    cast time; the range line drops out in space, SpaceRange being above its display cap) and
    no fuel (the tank takes astrofuel under VGE1). vacuumDescription is appended only when a
    loaded def can produce a space map, so players without Odyssey never read about it; it is an
    extension field rather than a patched description because a patch from a gated root would
    pull the description's DefInjected entry into that root and collide with the main tree's.

    Icons sit under the mod-scoped UI/Abilities/WarcasketShipcracker/. The VGE art root
    (Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Textures/) shadows both with purple copies at the same
    paths; keep the filenames in step.

    flightEffecter / spaceFlightEffecter are on the extension so a compat root can recolor
    them by patch; see EffecterDefs/BreachJumpFlame.xml and BreachBurnFlame.xml.

    thrusterGlowCurve maps cast progress (0 at the click, 1 at launch) to the opacity of the
    armor's thruster-glow render node: a quarter at 60% of the cast, most of it in the last
    third. Full for the flight, no fade-out after landing or an interrupted cast.
  -->
  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
    <defName>SCWC_BreachJump</defName>
    <label>breach jump</label>
    <description>Fire the armor's drop thrusters to jump to a location, landing hard enough to breach walls and hull plating. The jump is short but needs no clear path.</description>
    <abilityClass>ShipcrackerWarcasket.Ability_BreachJump</abilityClass>
    <gizmoClass>ShipcrackerWarcasket.Command_BreachJump</gizmoClass>
    <targetMode>Location</targetMode>
    <iconPath>UI/Abilities/WarcasketShipcracker/BreachJump</iconPath>
    <castTime>60</castTime>
    <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
    <keepCarryingThing>true</keepCarryingThing>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="ShipcrackerWarcasket.BreachJumpExtension">
        <fuelPerJump>20</fuelPerJump>
        <breachDamage>20</breachDamage>
        <breachArmorPenetration>0.15</breachArmorPenetration>
        <breachRadius>2</breachRadius>
        <roofPunchRadius>1</roofPunchRadius>
        <spaceFlightSpeedFactor>3</spaceFlightSpeedFactor>
        <spaceFlightMaxSeconds>4</spaceFlightMaxSeconds>
        <flightEffecter>SCWC_BreachJumpFlame</flightEffecter>
        <spaceFlightEffecter>SCWC_BreachBurnFlame</spaceFlightEffecter>
        <thrusterGlowCurve>
          <points>
            <li>(0, 0)</li>
            <li>(0.6, 0.25)</li>
            <li>(0.85, 0.65)</li>
            <li>(1, 1)</li>
          </points>
        </thrusterGlowCurve>
        <spaceIconPath>UI/Abilities/WarcasketShipcracker/BreachBurn</spaceIconPath>
        <vacuumDescription>In vacuum the burn has no range limit, but needs a clear line to the target.</vacuumDescription>
        <vacuumLabel>breach burn</vacuumLabel>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
</Defs>
